# GitLineage — production configuration template.
#
# Copy to a real environment file OUTSIDE the checkout, fill it in, and point
# the process supervisor at it. Every path below is persistent and lives outside
# the application directory on purpose.
#
#   install -d -m 0750 /srv/gitlineage/{cache,jobs,tmp,logs}
#   install -m 0640 gitlineage.env.example /srv/gitlineage/gitlineage.env
#   $EDITOR /srv/gitlineage/gitlineage.env
#
# The file is chmod 0640 and owned by the service user. It must never be
# committed and never be readable by the web user.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ runtime
NODE_ENV=production

# Bind on loopback when a reverse proxy or tunnel terminates TLS in front of the
# app, which is the recommended topology: the proxy is the only thing that needs
# to be reachable. Use 0.0.0.0 only when the platform's own firewall is the sole
# perimeter.
GITLINEAGE_HOST=127.0.0.1
GITLINEAGE_PORT=8080

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ storage
# PERSISTENT. Must be on a volume or disk that survives a redeploy. Nothing
# here may point inside the application checkout.
GITLINEAGE_CACHE=/srv/gitlineage/cache
GITLINEAGE_JOB_STORE=/srv/gitlineage/jobs

# Scratch space for the bounded git runner, read by git and by Node itself.
# Large enough for a shallow fetch of a big repository; disposable is acceptable.
TMPDIR=/srv/gitlineage/tmp

# Static client. Point at the build output in production, never at the source
# tree, so the served artefact is the one `npm run build` produced.
GITLINEAGE_CLIENT_DIR=/srv/gitlineage/app/dist/web

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- analysis
GITLINEAGE_DEPTH=200
GITLINEAGE_MAX_CANDIDATES=12
# A ceiling on one analysis. A five-minute job is normal for a large repository;
# this is the point at which a job is abandoned and marked retryable rather than
# running forever.
GITLINEAGE_ANALYSIS_TIMEOUT_MS=1800000

# Ceiling on the cheap revision probe every accepted request performs, so a slow
# GitHub cannot delay a 202.
GITLINEAGE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=8000

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ abuse
# Anonymous public deployment. These meter NEW work only: cached reads and
# result reads are never limited.
GITLINEAGE_RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=1
GITLINEAGE_RATE_LIMIT_PER_IP=5
GITLINEAGE_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=60000

# Global caps. 2 concurrent matches the measured behaviour of a single node:
# each analysis is I/O bound on GitHub and git, so more concurrency raises memory
# and quota spend without much throughput.
GITLINEAGE_MAX_CONCURRENT_ANALYSES=2
GITLINEAGE_MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH=20

# -------------------------------------------------------- client IP / proxy
# Leave EMPTY unless traffic is guaranteed to arrive through a proxy you control
# and which OVERWRITES this header.
#
#   Cloudflare named/proxy tunnel : cf-connecting-ip
#   Cloudflare quick tunnel       : cf-connecting-ip
#   nginx (proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr) : x-real-ip
#   Caddy (default)               : x-forwarded-for   (Caddy overwrites it)
#
# An EMPTY value means the socket address is used, which cannot be forged. That
# is the correct default. Setting this to a header that a client can also send
# lets anyone bypass the per-IP budget.
GITLINEAGE_TRUSTED_PROXY_HEADER=

# ---------------------------------------------------- public URL (optional)
# Documentation and link building only. Not asserted by the server, and never
# baked into the client bundle.
GITLINEAGE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=

# ------------------------------------------------------- kill switches
# Each of these disables a source of evidence or an outbound call. They exist for
# forensics and air-gapped diagnostics, and must stay at their default in a normal
# deployment: turning one on makes the graph less complete without saying so in
# the URL.
#
#GITLINEAGE_NO_GIT=
#GITLINEAGE_NO_REGISTRY=
#GITLINEAGE_NO_CLIENT=
# Extra outbound hosts, comma-separated, from configuration only. The base
# allowlist is four hosts; widening it from the environment is a deliberate
# decision and should be reviewed like one.
#GITLINEAGE_EXTRA_ALLOW_HOSTS=

# ---------------------------------------------------- GitHub credentials
# OPTIONAL. The server resolves a token in this order:
#   1. GITHUB_TOKEN or GH_TOKEN from the environment
#   2. the local `gh` credential store, if `gh` is installed
#   3. anonymous access (60 requests/hour)
#
# Supply it through the host's secret facility as GITHUB_TOKEN. Set
# GITLINEAGE_NO_CLI_TOKEN=1 to forbid the credential-store fallback on a host
# where `gh` is installed but should not be consulted.
#
# NEVER commit it, never make the env file readable beyond the service user, and
# never place it in any client-visible value. `/healthz` and `/api/contract`
# report whether a token is in use, never its value.
#GITHUB_TOKEN=
#GITLINEAGE_NO_CLI_TOKEN=1